    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Knowledge Graph separation — the method",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-29: *\"need replicable process for when KG gets too large to\nhandle and skills\"*, and on cat-harness: *\"follow same methodology/house\nrules/process\"*. This is that method. It was written down from what the\nbootstrap separation actually did and what went wrong on the way (bean `r3gy`,\n`xsqm`, and 94 separation beans surveyed), not from a plan.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean r3gy",
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "When — the signals, and none of them alone",
      "prov:value": "| signal | how it is measured |\n|---|---|\n| files and bytes per instance | `git ls-files \\| cut -d/ -f1 \\| sort \\| uniq -c` |\n| clone cost | `bun run cat health` → `repository-size` |\n| gate time a content change pays | `bun run cat gates` (the gate count and wall time) |\n| merge contention | commits per day on `main`; PRs re-conflicted before merge |\n| cohesion and cut of the candidate | `bun run cat kg:detangle` |\n| wrong-direction edges **within one instance** — modules bucketed into the proposed repos by path rule | `check:partition` (its root is ONE instance; read the scope it prints) |\n| wrong-direction edges **between instances** — checked against each one's declared `needs` | `bun run cat kg:detangle:direction`, blocking in CI (bean `p11x`) |\n| wrong-direction **references** — the prose axis, not the import axis | `check:reference-direction` |\n| what the tools would drag along | the import cone of the would-be tools package (`check:tools-closure` once it exists) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean p11x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "An example pointing up is a mention, not a dependency",
      "prov:value": "`check:reference-direction` holds that nothing names an instance that depends\non it. One kind of pointer does not break that rule: a lower layer citing a\nsource **as an example**, where the one copy of that source lives in a layer\nabove it (owner, 2026-10-30, smart-ra thread: \"one copy in smart-ra\", then\n\"A. Example is a mention\").",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "An example pointing up is a mention, not a dependency",
      "prov:value": "The case that settled it: the base IG layer's DTH document kind and DTH voice quote\nthe draft DPI-H Reference Architecture as evidence for their rules. The draft's\nlibrary entry is smart-ra's (the folio for that document, which builds on\nthe base IG layer). The base IG layer used to carry a second copy, and two copies of one key\nbroke the bibliography build. Now:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Preconditions — each was learned from a failure",
      "prov:value": "1. **Names agree before the cut** — directory, declared `name`, package name.\n   A rename after the cut is a cross-repository change.\n2. **One directory per instance**, so extraction is one move, not a sift.\n3. **Every gate that guards the boundary has been watched failing** — plant a\n   violation, see it red, remove it. Four boundary gates in this repository\n   passed while guarding nothing (`4j3h` could not fail, `q2wn` could not see\n   side-effect imports, `p11x` could not see across instances, `ymsu` was\n   repaired before it ran).\n4. **The owner's decisions are recorded in the bean** (the table below).\n5. **\"Generated output is the contract\" is written down** (`319n`): what\n   crosses the boundary is the generated file, and any tool may produce it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4j3h",
        "bean 319n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "An example pointing up is a mention, not a dependency",
      "prov:value": "## Preconditions — each was learned from a failure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The pair: a content repository and a tools repository",
      "prov:value": "Owner rulings that make the pattern (2026-09-29, bean `xsqm`):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xsqm",
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Staged content with no tools repository yet — the finding, not the silence",
      "prov:value": "An instance can be planned as a content repository before its `-tools` pair\nis authorised (the IRIS replica, 2026-09-30). Declare it — `separation: \"content\"` in\n`<name>.json`; the content half of an existing pair is read from the tools\ninstance's `supports` and needs nothing — and kg:audit's\n`content-instance-holds-code` records a finding naming every code file still\ninside it. It is a `minor` QA **warning**, not a failure, by owner ruling\n(2026-10-01: *\"QA warning. not failure.. ok b/c small # tools\"*): the owner\ntolerates the code *for now* (IRIS-specific tools may stay in the IRIS replica for now),\nand the warrant is that the tolerated set is small. It was `major` until then,\non the argument that FR-7 has no legitimate exceptions. A warning still names\neach file, so the violation is never silent. The remedy splits by what\nthe code is: **generic** code (it works for any instance of its kind — any\nDSpace catalogue, any PDF) moves into the platform and takes the instance root\nas an argument; **instance-specific** code waits for `<name>-tools`. Bean\n`eayu`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30",
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30",
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The stages",
      "prov:value": "| # | stage | lane | gate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Brief, measure the signals, claim | `authoring-agent` | signals in the bean; `bun run cat beans:claim <id>` |\n| 1–3 | Declare in place, detangle, isolate | `authoring-agent` | [`graph-detanglement`](graph-detanglement.md) — all its gates |\n| 4 | **Identity**: `name`, `version`, `iriBase`, `needs`, `nodeSchemas` in the declaration; move the base once | `platform-authoring-agent` | `iri:sync -- --from <old base>` then `iri:sync:check`; `check:node-iris` |\n| 5 | **Hosted outputs out** of the content | `platform-authoring-agent` | the content leak test's pending list is empty |\n| 6 | **Split content from tools**: create `<name>-tools/` as a sibling, move the code, cut its import cone | `platform-authoring-agent` | FR-7 (content holds no code); `check:tools-closure`; generated files byte-identical before and after |\n| 7 | **Publication plan**: every identifier the content mints is a file some step publishes, at `/v<major>/` | `publication-manager` | `check:node-iris`; the site layout in [`instance-publication`](../kg-core/instance-publication.md) §\"The release site\" |\n| 8 | **Rehearse standalone**: copy content + tools alone into a temporary directory and run the tools' checks there | `build-pipeline` | green with nothing else on the path; an empty tree exits non-zero |\n| 9 | **Authorise** — report what moves, sizes, what breaks, and wait | `administrator` | the owner's answer ([`deletion-requires-confirmation`](../../conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md)) |\n| 10 | **Seed**: the owner creates the repositories; once the source has settled, seed `main`, then the content and tools as reviewed PRs, with history | `administrator`, then `authoring-agent` | `bun run cat seed:ready --layer <name> --rehearse` answers `settled` for each layer, at seed time; then the seeding PRs reviewed and green |\n| 11 | **Parent consumes, additively**: pin (a SHA while staging, a version once released), repoint imports, keep the parent's copy. After any move of files between the pair, run the post-move sweep first ([below](#after-a-move-lands--the-post-move-sweep)) | `platform-authoring-agent` | the parent green with the dependency declared; `check:published-refs`; every gate in the sweep table |\n| 12 | **First release**: tag, publish `/v<major>/` | `publication-manager` | `check:version-bump`; every identifier dereferences ([`publish-verification`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/publish-verification.md)) |\n| 13 | **Cutover**: the one commit retiring the parent's copy into [`fsh-guts`](../kg-core/fsh-guts.md) as a verified archive (the deposit `state:seed --cutover` makes: it must extract to the exact tree removed, with a provenance note), deposited into the PARENT's fsh-guts before the removal, frozen, never refreshed or rendered: a relocation, not a deletion (owner, 2026-10-06; [`sub-kg-lifecycle`](sub-kg-lifecycle.md) stage 13 has the steps) | `administrator` | only after 11 and 12 are green; DONE only when `bun run cat separation:cutover:check --site`, run in the separated repository, exits 0 (Tool `separation-cutover-check`: mounts, declarations resolve, no monorepo wiring, layer direction, the site builds from the mounts alone) |\n| 14 | **Independent refinement**: each new release adopted by the parent as a reviewed step | `authoring-agent` | [`upstream-version-adoption`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/upstream-version-adoption.md) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "A seed is a snapshot: one commit that names the source sha, with no history\n(bean `iai8`). **Every open PR whose diff touches the layer when the snapshot\nis taken is orphaned into the monorepo**: after cutover its change is in\nneither the seed nor anywhere that reads it. Stage 8 asked whether the layer\nstands alone, but the tree has moved since. So `GW_SeedReady` sits between\ncreating the repositories and seeding them, and asks again:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean iai8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "| criterion | `not yet` when |\n|---|---|\n| heavy movers | an open PR labelled `heavy-mover` touches the layer or the next one up |\n| next layer | any open PR touches the next layer up, which imports this one |\n| layer load | more than five open PRs touch the layer |\n| moves | an open PR deletes a file in the layer, or renames one into or out of it. A generator's own names do not count: an `owned-tree` path in `merge-conflict-patterns.ts` (content-hashed payloads, rail data) is renamed by every regen, so moving one changes what no seeded path means (owner, 2026-10-06) |\n| standalone | `bun test` is red with only the layer and what it `needs` beside it, as sibling directories |\n| upward paths | a path DECLARED in the layer — a Tool module, a QA criterion source, a render target — resolves only in an instance above it, so it breaks the day the layer stands alone |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "These were the steward's hand-applied criteria (2026-10-02), generalised per\nlayer.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "**A test about the WHOLE CHECKOUT lives at the top (owner, 2026-10-06, \"Top-level\ninstance\"; bean `7zz1`).** A test that reads several sibling instances at\nonce, or the aggregate root itself (`.github/`, `.gitignore`, the root\ndeclaration, `beans/`, `todos/`, `memory/`, `fsh-guts/`), is red in every layer\nit is placed in, so it goes in the root instance's DECLARED test home —\n`folio-assistant-tests` in `folio-assistant.json`, at `test/` — never in a layer\nand never at a path a runner hardcodes. Whatever names every layer belongs at the\ntop, so each layer below stays standalone-green. Split a file when only some of\nits tests read the checkout, keep the fixture tests with their layer, compose\nthe moved paths from `ORIGIN_DIR` (the directory the test was written in), and\nmove a corpus describe whole when it carries a vacuity guard: a sibling left\nbehind passes standalone over nothing.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 7zz1",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "**A test reading an UPPER layer's files moves to that layer (owner, 2026-10-06,\non the tests that read the tools layer's files: move them to that layer).** It is\nred standing alone for the same reason, one level down: the file it reads is\nnot in its layer's closure. It goes in the upper layer's DECLARED test home,\nwhich may import the lower layer — never the reverse — and it is split, pointed\nback to and composed from `ORIGIN_DIR` exactly as above. Check first that the\nfile it reads really IS the upper layer's: a path written from the checkout root\n(`cat-harness/src/…` read relative to the working directory) is red standing\nalone over a file the layer does hold, and the fix there is to resolve it from\nthe test file, not to move it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "**A test that reads the checkout's GIT asks which of two things it is (owner,\n2026-10-06, \"Throwaway repository, plus moving the real-repo checks\").** A\nstandalone layer is a fresh clone with no `origin` and one commit, so a test\nhanded this checkout's remote, `HEAD` or `origin/main` fails there on a missing\ninput. A test of LOGIC that merely reads git — address derivation, an upload\nURL's shape, a commit IRI, resolving a short sha — builds a throwaway repository\nwhose facts it sets (`gitFixtureRepo` in cat-harness's\n`test/support/git-fixture.ts`) and passes that root, with every assertion\nexactly as strict; a function that resolves its root internally gains an\noptional root parameter defaulting to today's. A check that THIS repository is\nconfigured right — its own Pages address, its committed pages' banners — keeps\nits assertion verbatim and moves to the top-level test home above.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "**`upward paths` replaced `sibling discovery` (owner, 2026-10-04).** The old\ncriterion counted dependents that discovery could not find in a workspace of\nsibling clones. Discovery is checkout-local on purpose (`cmsl`), so that count\ncould never reach zero, and it counted *instances* where the risk is *paths*.\nOn cat-harness it read 3 while 0 of 134 declared paths resolved above the layer.\nCount what breaks, not what is out of sight.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean cmsl",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "**A seeding pair is not upward (owner, 2026-10-04).** When the code moved to\nthe tools layer, the harness's Tool nodes kept their `src/tools/*` paths and\nresolve into their implementer through `needs` (\"Trap 1\"), so the count read\n23 for the harness. The two are seeded in the same step, so none of those can\nbreak on seeding day. The HIGHER instance says so, `seedsWith: [<lower>]` in\nits declaration, because a lower instance naming one above it is the wrong\ndirection. `seed:ready` states such paths in its note and does not count\nthem; a path into any other instance above still counts.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Ready to seed? — asked at seed time, not at rehearsal",
      "prov:value": "- **The layer map is read off the declarations**: `livesAt.path` is the\n  directory, the longest `needs` chain is the depth, and the next layer is\n  every instance one level up that needs this one. Nothing in the tool names\n  a directory.\n- **Every threshold is in the decision table**,\n  `decisions/seed-readiness-gate.dmn`. The script works out each criterion's\n  verdict by evaluating the table with the other facts at zero, so changing\n  \"five\" is a one-line edit to the table.\n- **`heavy-mover` is a label a person applies** (owner, 2026-10-02). With\n  none on the layer, the criterion passes. If the label cannot be read, the\n  answer is `could-not-determine`.\n- **The rehearsal runs only on request.** Owner, 2026-10-02: *\"Optional, run\n  only on request with --rehearse.\"* It copies the layer and its `needs` into\n  a scratch workspace (~150 MB and ~8,000 tests for cat-harness) and refuses\n  to start with less than 3 GB free. Without `--rehearse`, the standalone\n  criterion is `could-not-determine`, so **`seed:ready` cannot answer\n  `settled` until a rehearsal has run.** That consequence is the one constant\n  `SETTLED_REQUIRES_REHEARSAL`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Identifiers and versions",
      "prov:value": "One `iriBase` and one `version` in the declaration. Identifiers a program reads\nand pages a person reads are both `<iriBase>v<major>/…`; the exact release is\nthe pin's (owner, 2026-10-23; `bootstrap-tools/schemas/release-iri.ts`). A base move is\n`bun run iri:sync -- --from <old base>`, once. A `$schema` tag carries its\nschema's own semver. The exported graph's own `@id` moves only when the new\nrepository actually publishes (`40fl`). A published node's identifier must be\nits file's path (`check:node-iris`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 40fl",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Versions of the pair — same scheme, same start, then independent",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-29: *\"on creation of new repo/staging dir, they use the same\nSEMVER for simplicity at time of split. then they are managed independently.\nsome tools may be able to manage several different versions / ranges of\nversions of the content.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Versions of the pair — same scheme, same start, then independent",
      "prov:value": "- **At the split, both start at the content's current version** — bootstrap\n  was `0.1.0`, so bootstrap-tools starts at `0.1.0`.\n- **After that each is versioned on its own**, by the same rules: semver, the\n  bump computed from the exported surface (`check:version-bump`).\n- **Tags are plain `v<major>.<minor>.<patch>` in each new repository** (owner,\n  2026-09-30): a standalone repository holds one instance, declared at its\n  root, so the tag needs no name. `check:version-bump` reads the plain form\n  only there; a repository of several instances — the parent while the pair\n  is staged — keeps `<name>-v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`, because a plain tag\n  could not say which instance it released.\n- **A tools release says which content versions it handles** as a list of\n  supported MAJOR versions (`bootstrap: [0]`), never a range expression —\n  `instance-versioning` rule 2 forbids range syntax, and within one major a\n  newer minor or patch only adds (`tagCompatible`). A tool asked to work on a\n  content major it does not list refuses rather than guesses.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "How the parent consumes the pair",
      "prov:value": "The owner ruled on 2026-10-06 (bean `0mpw`, `remote-mount.md`): **no git submodules, ever**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0mpw",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "How the parent consumes the pair",
      "prov:value": "### Separation lessons learned (2026-10-08, extended 2026-10-09)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-08",
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-08",
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Separation lessons learned (2026-10-08, extended 2026-10-09)",
      "prov:value": "1. **Downstream Gitignore Contract**: When remote mounts populate an instance directory in the consumer repository, the consumer's `.gitignore` must ignore the mounted paths. Otherwise, git treats external files as uncommitted local files. `index.config.json` automatically includes all `remoteMounts` paths in the generated `.gitignore`.\n2. **Folded Layer Aliases**: When an instance or subgraph is folded into another (e.g. `cat-openapi` folded into `cat-harness` as named subgraph `openapi`), existing external forks or historical dependencies may still carry `needs: [\"cat-openapi\"]`. `schemas/kg/harness-config.ts` maintains `FOLDED_INSTANCE_ALIASES` to resolve these transparently without breaking dependency graphs.\n3. **Asset Permission & License Validation**: Pre-separation audits must verify `library/withheld.json` and copyright gates. Materializing or mounting a separated catalogue without verified asset clearance causes 404s and broken links on published documentation.\n4. **NPM Manifest in the KG**: `package.json` is an authored pre-packaging asset in the Knowledge Graph (`role: \"package-manifest\"`), and `.tgz` release tarballs are tracked as `folio-binary-release/v1` state documents with SHA-256 integrity digests.\n5. **No Relative Directory Climbing Across Repositories**: In a monorepo, files routinely import siblings via `../../cat-harness/` or `../../bootstrap-tools/`. Once separated into standalone checkouts, climbing two or three levels (`../..` or `../../..`) escapes the repository boundary into `.claude/worktrees/` or the parent filesystem, immediately causing `Cannot find module` errors and test suite failures. All cross-repository imports MUST be authored as package imports (e.g. `@litlfred/cat-harness/...` or via package `exports`), or resolved through package specifiers / tsconfig paths, NEVER through escaping filesystem `../..` traversals.\n6. **No Fixed-Depth Repository Root Assumptions (`REPO`)**: Scripts in separated repositories often inherit `const REPO = resolve(import.meta.dir, \"..\", \"..\")`. In the monorepo, `scripts/../..` was the checkout root; in standalone repositories, `scripts/..` is the root, so `scripts/../..` escapes into parent worktrees. This causes scripts to either fail to locate `<instance>.json` or inadvertently scan sibling worktrees. Repository root resolution must be dynamic—searching upward for `<instance>.json`, `index.config.json`, or `.git`—rather than assuming a hardcoded directory depth.\n7. **Clean Standalone Manifest (`package.json`) and Tooling Scaffolding**: When extracting an instance to an upstream repository, `package.json` must be normalized:\n   - Operational commands must live under `\"scripts\"`, not leftover monorepo `\"checkoutScripts\"`.\n   - Script definitions must NOT hardcode monorepo subdirectory paths (e.g. `\"bun run cat-harness-tools/scripts/...\"` -> `\"bun run scripts/...\"`).\n   - A standalone `tsconfig.json` must be present to prevent `tsc` from walking up to the monorepo root.\n   - Explicit `dependencies` and `devDependencies` must be declared.\n8. **Fan-Out Recursion Guard in `declaringInstances`**: When a mounted dependency carries its own nested `remoteMounts`, consumer remote fan-out resolution must not recursively mount sub-instances into roots that are already locked mounts of the parent checkout. Without filtering (`!lockedMountPaths(checkout).has(rel)`), `remoteFanOut` re-mounts nested dependencies directly into the child checkout's directory, mutating its pristine checkout tree, inflating its file count, and causing `treeDigest` verification to fail.\n9. **Relative Directory Symlink Handling in Staging & Tarball Scripts**: In repositories containing internal symlinked directory trees (such as FHIR Implementation Guides with test structure links), recursive directory copy utilities (like `cpSync(..., { recursive: true })`) can trigger infinite self-copy recursion loops. Staging, site compilation, and packaging scripts must copy symlinks with `{ dereference: false }` or use archive utilities (such as `tar` or `rsync -a`) that preserve symlink references rather than traversing into directory cycles.\n10. **Purely Declarative Ontologies vs. Companion Toolsets (FR-7)**: Purely declarative base repositories (such as `litlfred/bootstrap`) must contain zero runtime execution code, zero test suites, and zero `package.json` manifests by architectural contract (FR-7). All graph compilation (JSON-LD export, BPMN diagram rendering, site staging, and schema validation) is executed by the companion tooling repository (`bootstrap-tools`). The declarative repository explicitly marks its render exemption (`renderExemption: true`) in its root manifest, and tooling scripts accept an explicit target repository argument (`--repo <dir>`) rather than expecting co-located execution.\n11. **Toolchain Decentralization (`package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `bunfig.toml`)**: Tools and harness subgraphs must possess full standalone toolchain autonomy. `package.json` must be a standalone package manifest (e.g. `@litlfred/<tools-layer>`), `bunfig.toml` defines test preloads per instance, and `tsconfig.json` must set `\"noEmit\": true` and omit `rootDir`/`outDir` to prevent `error TS6059: File is not under rootDir` when cross-subgraph schemas or utilities are imported. See [`bun-use`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/bun-use.md).\n12. **Monorepo Coordinator Demotion**: Once tools and code are extracted to their respective packages, the root `package.json` is demoted to a private coordinator (`\"private\": true`) with narrowed `tsconfig.json` (`test/**/*.ts`). The root platform coordinates development workspaces, mounts, and integration tests, but never directly exports or publishes tool implementations.\n13. **Ephemeral File Purging and Root Hygiene**: Ephemeral generated directories (`_kg/`, `build/`, `test-results/`) must NEVER be committed to the root repository or left unignored. Build outputs belong to the tool that produces them.\n14. **Instance Memory Preservation**: Root directories `beans/`, `todos/`, and `fsh-guts/` are the instance's own durable working memory (the agent's plan, the user's todo queue, and the archival store). They are never overlaid across instances, never extracted to downstream packages, and stay at root by design.\n15. **A cutover is not done until the instance has re-pointed and can publish itself (the IRIS replica, 2026-10-09)**: folio-assistant consumed the IRIS replica's repository remotely while the IRIS replica still declared `livesAt: { repository: \"litlfred/folio-assistant\", path: \"<iris-replica>\" }`, had no `iriBase`, and had never had stage 7 or 12. `livesAt` is not a comment: `remote-mount.ts` takes `livesAt.path` as the mount path and `seed-ready` reads it as \"still staged\". And `/<iris-replica>/` had only ever been a mount inside the parent's site build, so `litlfred.github.io/<iris-replica>/` served nothing. The generated pages also kept absolute links to the parent's paths (`folio-assistant/.../who-iris-approval/uploads/...`), which 404 once the bytes moved. Before stage 13: `livesAt` is gone, `iriBase` is declared, and the instance's own site builds from its own repository. Building that site exposed the next gap, that a downstream cannot compose a site without the harness's entire `docs/` graph, which is [Semantic subgraphs](../../../docs/proposals/semantic-subgraphs-2026-10-09.md).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09",
        "docs/proposals/semantic-subgraphs-2026-10-09.md"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Separation lessons learned (2026-10-08, extended 2026-10-09)",
      "prov:value": "16. **The replayer must never live inside a layer it replays (cat-harness cutover, 2026-10-09)**: every workflow in folio-assistant — and, through the reusable `folio-staging.yml@main`, every downstream folio's staging build — bootstrapped with `bun \"<platform>/cat-harness-tools/scripts/mount-from-lock.ts\"`. The cutover removed `cat-harness/` from the parent's tree, so the first step of every job failed with `Module not found \"folio-assistant/cat-harness-tools/scripts/mount-from-lock.ts\"` before any of the job's own work ran (measured on `litlfred/smart-ra#32`'s staging; fixed by folio-assistant#2518's dependency-free `.github/mount-from-lock.sh`, which fetches the pinned replayer). `mount-from-lock.ts` was written to break exactly this loop for `bootstrap-tools` (its own docblock: \"the tool that would fetch it cannot be loaded until it is there\") and then moved into a layer that is itself mounted. **Before stage 13**, grep every workflow the parent ships for paths into the directory being retired, and give the parent a bootstrap entry point that lives in the parent and needs nothing mounted.\n17. **A downstream's CI is part of \"green\" for a cutover**: a reusable workflow called `@main` (`uses: litlfred/folio-assistant/.github/workflows/folio-staging.yml@main`) runs the PARENT's current workflow in the DOWNSTREAM's repository. A cutover that is green in the parent can therefore be red in every folio at once, and the red lands on whatever pull request the folio author opens next — it reads as their failure. Stage 12's \"green\" includes one dispatched staging run of at least one downstream folio after the cutover commit.\n18. **A separated checkout must run its own tests and type-check its own subgraphs (cat-harness, 2026-10-09)**: measured in a fresh standalone clone, `scripts/tests/skill-coverage.test.ts` and `tools.test.ts` still read `<checkout>/../package.json` (`harness-schema-export.ts`, via `repoRootFor`) and fail with `ENOENT` outside the composed tree — lesson 6 by another route; and `tsconfig.json`'s `include` names `scripts/`, `schemas/`, … but not the named subgraphs `openapi/` and `archimate/`, so `tsc` was green while never reading them (both added to `include` in cat-harness#55; they type-check clean). A test or type-check that silently depends on the composition, or silently skips part of the repository, is not evidence the separated repository works.\n19. **The kinds a declaration is judged against come from the checkout being read, not from where the harness module sits (lesson 6, inside the graph-typology registry; 2026-10-12)**: `defaultGraphTypologies` took its `typologies/` root as two levels above `cat-harness/schemas/`. Inside the monorepo, or a downstream that mounts the harness, that is the checkout every `check:*` script reads from `cwd`; for a standalone cat-harness-tools run against `smart-ra` it was the directory of sibling clones, which held no `fhir-harness`, so `readDeclaration` threw *\"unknown graph typology fhir-artifact-index\"* over `smart-base.json`, a correct declaration, while the mounted copy of the same script passed. Two layouts, two answers about one file. The registry now reads the checkout under inspection first (`defaultTypologyRoots`; `$REPO_ROOT` still overrides), then its own; a kind both declare is shadowed and reported, never merged. Every path a declaration names is now resolved in one run by `check:declaration-resolution`, and `separation:cutover:check` uses it as its `declarations` condition. Which layout is canonical is still the owner's ruling: [Checkout layout](../../../docs/proposals/checkout-layout-2026-10-12.md).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "smart-ra#32",
        "folio-assistant#2518",
        "cat-harness#55",
        "2026-10-09",
        "2026-10-12",
        "docs/proposals/checkout-layout-2026-10-12.md"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09",
        "2026-10-12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "After a move lands — the post-move sweep",
      "prov:value": "Learned on cat-harness bean `70lx` stage 1a (cat-harness e29c6429, which moved\n`scripts/`, `src/`, `pipeline/`, most of `test/` and the archimate and\nopenapi scripts into the tools layer d8d42ab), and on the index re-pin that\nhad to follow it (folio-assistant #2524, superseded by #2529; bean\n`folio-assistant-beaf`, 2026-10-10). The move itself was one reviewed commit\nin each repository. **Making the repositories that consume the move work again\ntook about twenty more PRs across six repositories and a day.** Nearly all of\nthem were one of the classes below. Run the sweep after a move lands and\nbefore the parent re-pins (stage 11), and do not call the move done until\nevery gate in this table is green in a composed checkout at the matched pins.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 70lx",
        "#2524",
        "#2529",
        "2026-10-10"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "After a move lands — the post-move sweep",
      "prov:value": "| what still named the old home | the gate that catches it | how it was fixed in 70lx |\n|---|---|---|\n| A Tool node's `invoke.shell` | `kg:audit` criterion `tool-invoke-path-resolves` (CRITICAL; 43 of them) | cat-harness #84: the 47 invokes in `tools/index.ts` |\n| Prose and commands in skills, guides, READMEs, BPMN documentation, workflows | `check:command-paths` | cat-harness #99: 170 lines in 83 files |\n| A script's own usage string | `check:usage-paths` | cat-harness-tools #41 |\n| Printed and RUN commands: \"Run: …\" remedies, generated banners, shell hooks, an e2e global setup that ran an old path | `check:published-instance-exports`, `check:invocation-parity`, `security:gate` (all three matched old paths by text), and the unit tests | cat-harness-tools #39, #43 (429 strings in 183 files) |\n| A wrapper generator's list of the scripts it wraps | `bat:sync` / `bat:sync:check` (the writer errored on the first missing file) | cat-harness-tools #53 |\n| Partition rules naming moved files | `check:partition` (\"exact rule(s) name a file that is not in …\") | cat-harness-tools #55: 332 dead rules removed (owner: \"2y\") |\n| A kind-validator node pointing at a moved module | `check:kind-validators:require-all` | open: how a node in one layer names a module in the other |\n| A writer's claims in `qa-refresh`: sidecars that used to be committed files the writer *rewrites* became output it *writes* | `qa:refresh` (\"N file(s) no declared writer claims\") | cat-harness-tools #27 |\n| A visualiser route a generator computed by hand (the glossary page moved under its declared route) | `uml:overview` inside `skill:register` (\"no glossary page at …\") | cat-harness-tools #27: `declaredRoute(<core>, \"glossary-page\")` |\n| A browser bundle importing a node-only module through a package import | `navbar:assets` (\"Browser polyfill for module node:url …\") | cat-harness #98 + cat-harness-tools #49: the constant moved into a node-free module |\n| A directory declared inside another declared directory in the receiving layer | `check:layout-norms` (it stopped `qa:refresh`) | cat-harness-tools #54: `health/` out of the declared `test/` (owner: option A) |\n| A file left in BOTH layers (`schemas/adjudication.ts` and `schemas/materialization.ts` were in cat-harness and in folio-assistant-core) | `slice:sqlite` / `slice:sqlite:check` (the KG export mints the same IRI twice and the slice dies on a UNIQUE constraint); `node-kinds:check` and `kg:export` do not refuse a duplicate on their own | delete the copy the move should have removed, in the layer that no longer owns it: folio-assistant-core#37 took the SWE-Debate schemas into core's `adjudication.ts`, cat-harness#106 removed the harness copies (archived to `fsh-guts/retired/`), cat-harness-tools#66 the stray `scripts/cache-index.ts` |\n| Paired artefacts a move split across repositories (`review-comments`, `glossary-terms` to folio-assistant-core; the GRADE lists to smart-base) | `skills:docs` (\"page(s) produced by NO source\"), `check:declared-dirs` (\"absent — declared and not on disk\") | pin the receiving commits WITH the removing one (below) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "folio-assistant-core#37",
        "cat-harness#106",
        "cat-harness-tools#66"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Pin the pair together, and record each consent first-hand",
      "prov:value": "**A move that removes files from one repository must be pinned together with\nthe commit that adds them to the receiving one.** cat-harness #81/#82 moved\ntwo skills out to the content core and six code lists to a content instance\nabove it; a parent pinning the new cat-harness with the OLD pins of those two\nreceiving repositories had those artefacts in neither, and the gates said so\nonly indirectly. The fix was to re-pin both receivers (their #20 and #27) in\nthe same re-pin. The general\nform: before a re-pin, list what each new commit removes and confirm the\nreceiving repository's pin contains it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-29",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Pin the pair together, and record each consent first-hand",
      "prov:value": "**Every pin is a trust decision with its own consent** (rule H8,\n`remote-mount`): `trust.consent` names who, when, the exact ref and the\nevidence, and `mount:remote` refuses a ref nobody consented to. A consent\nrelayed by another agent is not the owner's consent, so it is not recorded\nfrom the relay alone. In 70lx the session wrote no consent record until the\nowner's answer to a question naming the exact SHAs was relayed verbatim with\nits time. A standing consent (\"pin any main commit of these repositories that\nincludes a fix merged in this session, listed in the PR\") covers only the\nrepositories and the window it names, and each pin made under it is listed\nwhere the owner will read it. When a consented ref turns out not to do (a\nconsented `main` with no declaration of the instance), do not substitute\nanother ref: keep the previous pin and report it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-30",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The order that worked, and the rules for several sessions at once",
      "prov:value": "- **Hold pushes on a branch another session is superseding**; hand over what\n  is unpushed instead of racing it.\n- **Announce which gates each session takes** before starting, and re-check\n  the open PRs and recent merges of a repository before opening one there.\n- **Verify on the lock of the PR that will land**, in a fresh scratch copy,\n  never on another session's checkout.\n- **A measurement-only workaround stays local** (for 70lx, a baseline entry\n  for the layout-norms defect, needed to run `qa:refresh` while the owner\n  decided), is never committed, and is deleted once the real fix lands."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. bootstrap + bootstrap-tools",
      "prov:value": "- Stages 1–5: bean `r3gy` groups A–E (#1486, #1503) — wrong facts, folio-only\n  names, root-relative paths, graph typologies and `$schema` tags and QA out, IRIs\n  under `https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/` with semver.\n- Stage 6: bean `xsqm` — `bootstrap-tools/` re-created as a sibling; the Zod\n  source moved down; import cone from 19 files / 11,577 lines to 12 / 2,249,\n  `zod` only; `check:tools-closure` and `check:node-iris` added, each watched\n  failing on a planted violation.\n- Next: the README and diagram writers join bootstrap-tools; the publication\n  plan; the standalone rehearsal; then the owner's authorisation.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean r3gy",
        "bean xsqm",
        "#1486",
        "#1503"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/kg-separation.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. bootstrap + bootstrap-tools",
      "prov:value": "### 2. cat-harness + the tools layer (completed 2026-10-08)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-08"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
